{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/hypergraphs\/incidencegraphview"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:11Hypergraphs18IncidenceGraphViewV","title":"IncidenceGraphView","modules":[{"name":"Hypergraphs"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"struct","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"IncidenceGraphView","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"IncidenceGraphView","kind":"identifier"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"IncidenceGraphView.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView.swift#L50"}},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView"},"topicSections":[{"title":"Structures","anchor":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/Edges-swift.struct","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/IncidentEdgeIndices","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/Neighbors"],"generated":true},{"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/init(base:)"],"generated":true},{"title":"Instance Properties","anchor":"Instance-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/base","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/edgeCount","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/edgeIndexBound","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/edges-swift.property","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/vertexCount","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/vertexIndexBound","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/vertices"],"generated":true},{"title":"Instance Methods","anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/contains(_:)","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/contains(edge:)","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/degree(of:)","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/degree(ofIndex:)","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/edgeIndex(of:)","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/endpointIndices(ofEdgeAt:)","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/incidentEdgeIndices(ofIndex:)","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/incidentEdges(of:)","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/incidentEdges(ofIndex:)","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/neighborIndices(ofIndex:)","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/neighbors(of:)","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/oppositeVertex(to:acrossEdgeAt:)","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/vertex(atIndex:)","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/vertexIndex(of:)"],"generated":true},{"title":"Type Aliases","anchor":"Type-Aliases","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/IncidentEdges","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/NeighborIndices","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/Vertex"],"generated":true},{"title":"Default Implementations","anchor":"Default-Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/Graph-Implementations"],"generated":true}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"IncidenceGraphView","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Base","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Base","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hypergraph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols10HypergraphP","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Hypergraph"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Edges."}]},{"type":"text","text":" Edge position "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"q"},{"type":"text","text":" is incidence number "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"q"},{"type":"text","text":": the incidences hyperedge by hyperedge, in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"index order, and within a hyperedge in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"memberIndices"},{"type":"text","text":" order. So "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges[q]"},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UndirectedEdge(i, n + p)"},{"type":"text","text":", the rows of the hyperedge side are contiguous ranges, and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"per-incidence array (a weight of a vertex in a hyperedge) is indexed by edge position. A view"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is a snapshot, so its own positions never change, but they are valid for the hypergraph only"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"until its next mutation: the view of the mutated hypergraph numbers the incidences afresh (on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":", inserting one cell shifts every later incidence by one), and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"per-incidence array must be rebuilt for it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"The LabeledGraph law.","type":"text"}]},{"text":" Every index member reads the base’s rows:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"neighborIndices(ofIndex: i)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"incidentHyperedgeIndices(ofIndex: i)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" shifted by n, and of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"n + p","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" it is ","type":"text"},{"code":"memberIndices(ofHyperedgeAt: p)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". So ","type":"text"},{"code":"Traversal","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Connectivity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"ShortestPaths","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and the rest run on the view without hashing a vertex. ","type":"text"},{"code":"_withIncidentIndexRows","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"writes the view’s rows out once per call from the base’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"_withIncidenceRows","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"O(n + m + p), so whole-graph algorithms (components, bridges, cut vertices) run at an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"adjacency-list copy’s speed on every base.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Costs.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" The view keeps each hyperedge’s first incidence number, so a hyperedge’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"incidentEdges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a range, O(1). On ","type":"text"},{"code":"UndirectedIncidenceList","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which stores its incidences,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every read is O(1) plus the row. On any other base, ","type":"text"},{"code":"edges[q]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"endpointIndices(ofEdgeAt:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"binary-search the hyperedge and find the member by its rank (","type":"text"},{"code":"_memberIndex(atRank:…)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"),","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"O(log m + ⌈n\/64⌉) on ","type":"text"},{"code":"IncidenceMatrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and O(log m + k) by default, and a vertex’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"incidentEdges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" finds its place in each of its hyperedges: O(d·⌈n\/64⌉) on ","type":"text"},{"code":"IncidenceMatrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which counts bits, and O(Σ k) over them on a base without a faster ","type":"text"},{"code":"_memberRank","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BipartiteGraph(h.incidenceGraph, left: 0 ..< h.vertexCount)"},{"type":"text","text":" gives the bipartite structure,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and the view’s components restricted to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0 ..< n"},{"type":"text","text":" are the hypergraph’s."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An undirected hypergraph’s incidence graph, read lazily from its storage: a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Graph"},{"type":"text","text":" on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0 ..< n + m"},{"type":"text","text":" whose vertex "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i < n"},{"type":"text","text":" is the hypergraph’s vertex index "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i"},{"type":"text","text":" and whose vertex "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"n + p"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is hyperedge "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"p"},{"type":"text","text":", with an edge "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"{i, n + p}"},{"type":"text","text":" for each incidence. It is bipartite and simple"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(vertices on the left, hyperedges on the right), an empty hyperedge is an isolated vertex, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it loses nothing."}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"references":{"doc://Hypergraphs/documentation/Hypergraphs/IncidenceGraphView/edges-swift.property":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/edges-swift.property","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"edges"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"IncidenceGraphView","preciseIdentifier":"s:11Hypergraphs18IncidenceGraphViewV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Base"},{"kind":"text","text":">."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Edges","preciseIdentifier":"s:11Hypergraphs18IncidenceGraphViewV5EdgesV"}],"title":"edges","url":"\/documentation\/hypergraphs\/incidencegraphview\/edges-swift.property","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every incidence, at its number. O(1)."}]},"doc://Hypergraphs/documentation/Hypergraphs/IncidenceGraphView":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView","url":"\/documentation\/hypergraphs\/incidencegraphview","kind":"symbol","title":"IncidenceGraphView","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"IncidenceGraphView"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An und